Gunterdown dictionary data
=========================
The bundled fr/en/ja/zh/ko lexicons are adapted from FrequencyWords by Hermit
Dave, derived from OpenSubtitles 2018 via OPUS.
Source repository: https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords
Pinned revision: 525f9b560de45753a5ea01069454e72e9aa541c6

The content is licensed Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
International (CC BY-SA 4.0), separately from Gunterdown's MIT-licensed code.
License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
Full license text: src/gunterdown/data/dicts/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt

Adaptations by Gunterdown: token filtering, case folding, apostrophe
normalization, duplicate merging, original MIT vocabulary additions from
SUPPLEMENT.json, and conversion to compressed JSON.
The adapted lexicons are distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Per-language source
URLs, source checksums, counts and the pinned revision are recorded in
src/gunterdown/data/dicts/SOURCES.json and <language>.LICENSE.txt. Compressed data
checksums are recorded in SHA256SUMS. No endorsement by the source is implied.

No Wiktextract, JMDict, CC-CEDICT, KAIST or Noto font data is bundled.
Frequency lists come from subtitles and may contain colloquial forms, names
and transcription errors. They are not normative spelling dictionaries.

Python and curses are system dependencies. Pandoc, XeLaTeX, aspell and lpr
are optional external programs; none is bundled.
